      {
        "id": "Constitutional Amendment",
        "title": "Increasing funding to school districts",
        "summary": "Proposed by the Legislature (Laws 2026, chapter 114), this amendment rewrites the Minnesota Constitution's permanent school fund section so the fund is managed as a perpetual resource designed to pay out annual distributions to school districts while preserving its purchasing power. If adopted, a companion law sets each year's distribution at 4.5 percent of the fund's average net asset value over the previous three fiscal years, starting with aid paid in fiscal year 2028. Under Minnesota law, leaving this question blank counts the same as a No vote.",
        "yesMeans": "You approve changing the Constitution to increase payouts from the permanent school fund to all school districts, effective July 1, 2027.",
        "noMeans": "You reject the amendment, and the permanent school fund keeps its current constitutional rules and payout method.",
